  "riskClass": "medium",
  "title": "WhatsApp deep links use phone numbers without +91 country code prefix",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: Business Logic. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. CustomersPage WhatsApp link (line 252) uses `c.phone.replace(/[^0-9+]/g, '')` to clean the phone number, but if the stored phone number is a bare 10-digit Indian number (e.g., '9876543210'), the wa.me link becomes `wa.me/9876543210` which WhatsApp may not resolve correctly - it requires the international format `wa.me/919876543210`. The same pattern appears in InvoicesPage (line 383) and PurchaseOrdersPage (line 324) where `phone.replace(/\\D/g, '')` strips everything non-numeric. If the phone stored is '9876543210' (10 digits), the link will be `wa.me/9876543210` without country code.",
